From 2a94b472aa3a6117e87796ac9a68361f53d3ea5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 00:38:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(cad): LLM+CAD made honest and fast -- stale
 stand-ins remade, asset.cad status, run records, warm --scad

- Stale llm_scad variants: a template stored while OpenSCAD was missing, offline, lost to a restart, or before its
  CAD model landed (warm --scad in another process) is remade on the next request (assets.scad_stale; the endpoints
  wait up to 15 s for the rebuild). A failure counts for its model for an hour (scad.failed.json).
- asset.cad on llm_scad answers (part.json?mode=, POST /parts/{id}/model + top-level cad, X-Asset-Cad):
  {status writing|ready|failed|none, started_at, eta_s, made_by, seconds, cost_usd, reason}; cross-process via
  scad.writing.json. At most 2 live CAD runs at once.
- meshgen.grok_scad_run: records calls, fixes, seconds, cost, tokens and the raw bbox error (scad.json /
  scad.failed.json); OpenSCAD errors now carry the model-side TRACE lines (the library's line numbers were shown as
  the model's); ASSET_SCAD_EFFORT (default "low"), ASSET_SCAD_FIXES, ASSET_SCAD_SAMPLES; profile-based ETA/cost table.
- Default writer: grok-4.7 at low effort (measured 34-127 s, $0.016-0.056 a part vs 216-400 s, $0.10-0.20 at its
  default effort, similar geometry); grok-4.20 non-reasoning is 9-19 s but flatter shapes.
- python -m server.warm --scad: catalog items with a model + SCAD_DEMO_PARTS, 3 at a time, resumable, failures
  recorded, variant rebuilt, --estimate / --retry-failed / --sites / --scad-match / --scad-parts.
- server/experiments/scad_bench.py (per-model timing) and cad_compare.py (side-by-side renders + table).
- tests/test_cad.py: 15 (OpenSCAD and the LLM stubbed) + 1 opt-in live.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
